"use strict";(self.webpackChunkseriousjul_github_io=self.webpackChunkseriousjul_github_io||[]).push([["9602"],{5272(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"2026-11-11-actual-budget-actual-26-11-0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-actual-budget-actual-26-11-0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/SeriousJul/seriousjul.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-11-11-actual-budget-actual-26-11-0-release.mdx","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-11-actual-budget-actual-26-11-0-release.mdx","title":"Actual Budget 26.11.0 ships automatic syncing and breaking SimpleFin change","description":"Actual Budget released version 26.11.0 on 2026-11-02, its latest stable release. The update adds automatic bank syncing at a chosen interval, custom reports grouped by tags, and a more customizable sidebar, alongside per-budget SimpleFIN credentials and performance optimizations for large budgets. It also introduces a breaking change: custom SimpleFIN bridges on private networks now require a server allowlist.","date":"2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Project","permalink":"/news/tags/project","description":"Posts about projects and their releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"Actual Budget","permalink":"/news/tags/actual-budget","description":"Posts about the Actual Budget personal finance app"}],"readingTime":0.77,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Julien Antony","title":"Systems tinkerer","url":"https://seriousjul.github.io","page":{"permalink":"/news/authors/seriousjul"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/seriousjul"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/seriousjul.png","key":"seriousjul"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Actual Budget 26.11.0 ships automatic syncing and breaking SimpleFin change","authors":["seriousjul"],"tags":["project","actual-budget"],"slug":"2026-11-11-actual-budget-actual-26-11-0-release"},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"Coder v2.38.7 becomes latest stable as v2.39 mainline ships","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-coder-2-38-7-stable"}},"content":"Actual Budget released version 26.11.0 on 2026-11-02, its latest stable release. The update adds automatic bank syncing at a chosen interval, custom reports grouped by tags, and a more customizable sidebar, alongside per-budget SimpleFIN credentials and performance optimizations for large budgets. It also introduces a breaking change: custom SimpleFIN bridges on private networks now require a server allowlist.\\n\\n## Releases\\n- v26.11.0 released on 2026-11-02, adding automatic bank syncing at a chosen interval, custom reports grouped by tags, and more customizable sidebar navigation ([source](https://github.com/actualbudget/actual/releases/tag/v26.11.0)).\\n- The same release includes per-budget SimpleFIN credentials and performance optimizations for large budgets ([source](https://github.com/actualbudget/actual/releases/tag/v26.11.0)).\\n\\n## Fixes and other\\n- Breaking change in v26.11.0 (2026-11-02): custom SimpleFIN bridges on private networks now require a server allowlist ([source](https://github.com/actualbudget/actual/releases/tag/v26.11.0)).\\n\\n## Sources\\n- https://github.com/actualbudget/actual/releases/tag/v26.11.0"},{"id":"2026-11-11-coder-2-38-7-stable","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-coder-2-38-7-stable","editUrl":"https://github.com/SeriousJul/seriousjul.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-11-11-coder-2-38-7-stable.mdx","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-11-coder-2-38-7-stable.mdx","title":"Coder v2.38.7 becomes latest stable as v2.39 mainline ships","description":"Coder moved the 2.38 line to the latest stable release with v2.38.7 on November 10, 2026, carrying a breaking change that validates workspace app URLs on the server. The v2.39 mainline line advanced in the same window: v2.39.0 shipped on November 3 with breaking changes, and v2.39.1 followed on November 10 as a patch release.","date":"2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Project","permalink":"/news/tags/project","description":"Posts about projects and their releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"Coder","permalink":"/news/tags/coder","description":"Posts about the Coder self-hosted development environment"}],"readingTime":1.39,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Julien Antony","title":"Systems tinkerer","url":"https://seriousjul.github.io","page":{"permalink":"/news/authors/seriousjul"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/seriousjul"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/seriousjul.png","key":"seriousjul"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Coder v2.38.7 becomes latest stable as v2.39 mainline ships","authors":["seriousjul"],"tags":["project","coder"],"slug":"2026-11-11-coder-2-38-7-stable"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Actual Budget 26.11.0 ships automatic syncing and breaking SimpleFin change","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-actual-budget-actual-26-11-0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Coder 2.39 mainline lands with breaking changes and wide stable backports","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-coder-v239-mainline-releases"}},"content":"Coder moved the 2.38 line to the latest stable release with v2.38.7 on November 10, 2026, carrying a breaking change that validates workspace app URLs on the server. The v2.39 mainline line advanced in the same window: v2.39.0 shipped on November 3 with breaking changes, and v2.39.1 followed on November 10 as a patch release.\\n\\n## Releases\\n\\n- v2.38.7 (Nov 10, 2026): now the latest stable release (\\"Stable since November 10, 2026\\"). Breaking change: validate workspace app URLs on the server (#31262). Also fixes: ignore retired OAuth2 scopes such as task:* (#31117) and tighten up database connection errors (#31850). Source: https://github.com/coder/coder/releases/tag/v2.38.7\\n- v2.39.0 (Nov 3, 2026): November mainline release. Includes breaking changes, such as the connection log migration that blocks reads and writes during the rewrite of the connection_logs table (#30466). Coder advises enterprise users without a staging environment to stay on the latest stable release while 2.39 is refined. Source: https://github.com/coder/coder/releases/tag/v2.39.0\\n- v2.39.1 (Nov 10, 2026): mainline patch release on the 2.39 line, fixing tightened-up database connection errors (#31850) and backporting release calendar and install version documentation refresh for v2.39.0 (#31716). Source: https://github.com/coder/coder/releases/tag/v2.39.1\\n\\n## Fixes and other\\n\\n- Server-side validation of workspace app URLs lands in v2.38.7 as a breaking fix, so misconfigured workspace app URLs are now rejected by the server (https://github.com/coder/coder/releases/tag/v2.38.7).\\n- Database connection error handling was tightened on both the 2.38 and 2.39 lines via #31850 (https://github.com/coder/coder/releases/tag/v2.39.1).\\n\\n## Sources\\n\\n- https://github.com/coder/coder/releases/tag/v2.38.7\\n- https://github.com/coder/coder/releases/tag/v2.39.0\\n- https://github.com/coder/coder/releases/tag/v2.39.1"},{"id":"2026-11-11-coder-v239-mainline-releases","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-coder-v239-mainline-releases","editUrl":"https://github.com/SeriousJul/seriousjul.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-11-11-coder-v239-mainline-releases.mdx","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-11-coder-v239-mainline-releases.mdx","title":"Coder 2.39 mainline lands with breaking changes and wide stable backports","description":"Coder shipped a new mainline v2.39.0 on Nov 3 with breaking changes, followed by v2.39.1 on Nov 10, while the stable lines all moved: v2.38.6 closed security advisory GHSA-cv23-7vc5-jfh7, and v2.38.7 became the new latest stable with a breaking change that validates workspace app URLs on the server. Backport releases v2.37.11 and v2.34.19 followed on Nov 10.","date":"2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Project","permalink":"/news/tags/project","description":"Posts about projects and their releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"Coder","permalink":"/news/tags/coder","description":"Posts about the Coder self-hosted development environment"}],"readingTime":1.9,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Julien Antony","title":"Systems tinkerer","url":"https://seriousjul.github.io","page":{"permalink":"/news/authors/seriousjul"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/seriousjul"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/seriousjul.png","key":"seriousjul"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Coder 2.39 mainline lands with breaking changes and wide stable backports","authors":["seriousjul"],"tags":["project","coder"],"slug":"2026-11-11-coder-v239-mainline-releases"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Coder v2.38.7 becomes latest stable as v2.39 mainline ships","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-coder-2-38-7-stable"},"nextItem":{"title":"egui 0.37.0 ships colored emoji","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-egui-0-37-0-colored-emoji"}},"content":"Coder shipped a new mainline v2.39.0 on Nov 3 with breaking changes, followed by v2.39.1 on Nov 10, while the stable lines all moved: v2.38.6 closed security advisory GHSA-cv23-7vc5-jfh7, and v2.38.7 became the new latest stable with a breaking change that validates workspace app URLs on the server. Backport releases v2.37.11 and v2.34.19 followed on Nov 10.\\n\\n## Releases\\n\\n- **v2.39.0** (Nov 3) - New mainline release on the 2.39 track. Breaking changes include a connection-log table migration that blocks reads and writes ([#30466](https://github.com/coder/coder/pull/30466)); Coder advises enterprise users without staging to wait for the latest stable. Source: [release page](https://github.com/coder/coder/releases/tag/v2.39.0)\\n- **v2.39.1** (Nov 10) - Mainline patch on the 2.39 track that tightens database connection errors ([#31850](https://github.com/coder/coder/pull/31850)) and backports release calendar and install version documentation refreshes. Source: [release page](https://github.com/coder/coder/releases/tag/v2.39.1)\\n- **v2.38.6** (Nov 3) - Stable line release marked \\"Stable (since November 03, 2026)\\"; bug fixes include bumping gomarkdown/markdown to fix security advisory [GHSA-cv23-7vc5-jfh7](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-cv23-7vc5-jfh7), plus dependency updates (chi v5.5.0, bundled Terraform 1.17.1). Source: [release page](https://github.com/coder/coder/releases/tag/v2.38.6)\\n- **v2.38.7** (Nov 10) - Now the latest stable release. Breaking change: workspace app URLs are validated on the server ([#31262](https://github.com/coder/coder/pull/31262)). Also fixes the server ignoring retired OAuth2 scopes such as `task:*` ([#31117](https://github.com/coder/coder/pull/31117)) and tightens database connection errors. Source: [release page](https://github.com/coder/coder/releases/tag/v2.38.7)\\n- **v2.37.11** (Nov 10) - Backport on the 2.37 line of server-side workspace app URL validation and tightened database connection error handling, plus the session-token restriction to trusted app links in `coder open app`. Source: [release page](https://github.com/coder/coder/releases/tag/v2.37.11)\\n- **v2.34.19** (Nov 10) - Backport on the 2.34 line of the same server-side app URL validation and database connection error fixes. Source: [release page](https://github.com/coder/coder/releases/tag/v2.34.19)\\n\\n## Sources\\n\\n- https://github.com/coder/coder/releases/tag/v2.39.0\\n- https://github.com/coder/coder/releases/tag/v2.39.1\\n- https://github.com/coder/coder/releases/tag/v2.38.6\\n- https://github.com/coder/coder/releases/tag/v2.38.7\\n- https://github.com/coder/coder/releases/tag/v2.37.11\\n- https://github.com/coder/coder/releases/tag/v2.34.19"},{"id":"2026-11-11-egui-0-37-0-colored-emoji","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-egui-0-37-0-colored-emoji","editUrl":"https://github.com/SeriousJul/seriousjul.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-11-11-egui-0-37-0-colored-emoji.mdx","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-11-egui-0-37-0-colored-emoji.mdx","title":"egui 0.37.0 ships colored emoji","description":"egui released version 0.37.0 on 2026-10-15, bringing colored emoji with full system glyph rendering, a new CompletionPopup autocomplete widget, and an experimental theme customization system. The release also adds MP4 video recording for integration tests and ships breaking changes, so upgrading projects should expect API and feature-flag adjustments.","date":"2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Project","permalink":"/news/tags/project","description":"Posts about projects and their releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"egui","permalink":"/news/tags/egui","description":"Posts about the egui GUI framework"}],"readingTime":0.61,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Julien Antony","title":"Systems tinkerer","url":"https://seriousjul.github.io","page":{"permalink":"/news/authors/seriousjul"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/seriousjul"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/seriousjul.png","key":"seriousjul"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"egui 0.37.0 ships colored emoji","authors":["seriousjul"],"tags":["project","egui"],"slug":"2026-11-11-egui-0-37-0-colored-emoji"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Coder 2.39 mainline lands with breaking changes and wide stable backports","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-coder-v239-mainline-releases"},"nextItem":{"title":"Egui 0.37.0 lands colored emoji and glyph rendering","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-egui-0370-colored-emojis"}},"content":"egui released version 0.37.0 on 2026-10-15, bringing colored emoji with full system glyph rendering, a new CompletionPopup autocomplete widget, and an experimental theme customization system. The release also adds MP4 video recording for integration tests and ships breaking changes, so upgrading projects should expect API and feature-flag adjustments.\\n\\n## Releases\\n\\n- On 2026-10-15, egui released version 0.37.0, headlined by colored emoji and full system glyph rendering. The release adds the CompletionPopup autocomplete widget, an experimental theme customization system, and MP4 video recording for integration tests. It also includes breaking changes: default_fonts is no longer a default feature, and new Id APIs were introduced. Source: https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0\\n\\n## Sources\\n\\n- https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0"},{"id":"2026-11-11-egui-0370-colored-emojis","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-egui-0370-colored-emojis","editUrl":"https://github.com/SeriousJul/seriousjul.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-11-11-egui-0370-colored-emojis.mdx","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-11-egui-0370-colored-emojis.mdx","title":"Egui 0.37.0 lands colored emoji and glyph rendering","description":"Egui released version 0.37.0 (\\"Colored emojis!\\") on 2026-10-15. The release adds rendering of any system glyph, including colored emojis and non-Latin scripts, through new GlyphRasterizer and FontProvider APIs, and ships a CompletionPopup widget for TextEdit autocomplete.","date":"2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Project","permalink":"/news/tags/project","description":"Posts about projects and their releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"egui","permalink":"/news/tags/egui","description":"Posts about the egui GUI framework"}],"readingTime":0.76,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Julien Antony","title":"Systems tinkerer","url":"https://seriousjul.github.io","page":{"permalink":"/news/authors/seriousjul"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/seriousjul"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/seriousjul.png","key":"seriousjul"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Egui 0.37.0 lands colored emoji and glyph rendering","authors":["seriousjul"],"tags":["project","egui"],"slug":"2026-11-11-egui-0370-colored-emojis"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"egui 0.37.0 ships colored emoji","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-egui-0-37-0-colored-emoji"},"nextItem":{"title":"Gadgetbridge 2026.11.0 and 2026.11.1 land new device support and fixes","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-gadgetbridge-november-stable-releases"}},"content":"Egui released version 0.37.0 (\\"Colored emojis!\\") on 2026-10-15. The release adds rendering of any system glyph, including colored emojis and non-Latin scripts, through new GlyphRasterizer and FontProvider APIs, and ships a CompletionPopup widget for TextEdit autocomplete.\\n\\n## Releases\\n- 2026-10-15: egui 0.37.0 (\\"Colored emojis!\\") released, the latest stable version of the crate ([source](https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0)).\\n\\n## Features\\n- Any system glyph can now be rendered, including colored emojis and non-Latin scripts, via the new GlyphRasterizer and FontProvider APIs (0.37.0) ([source](https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0)).\\n- New CompletionPopup widget provides autocomplete support for TextEdit (0.37.0) ([source](https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0)).\\n- Experimental widget theme plugin system introduced (0.37.0) ([source](https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0)).\\n- egui_kittest can now record mp4 videos of integration tests (0.37.0) ([source](https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0)).\\n\\n## Sources\\n- https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0"},{"id":"2026-11-11-gadgetbridge-november-stable-releases","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-gadgetbridge-november-stable-releases","editUrl":"https://github.com/SeriousJul/seriousjul.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-11-11-gadgetbridge-november-stable-releases.mdx","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-11-gadgetbridge-november-stable-releases.mdx","title":"Gadgetbridge 2026.11.0 and 2026.11.1 land new device support and fixes","description":"Gadgetbridge released two stable versions within the past month. 2026.11.0 (released 2026-11-03) adds initial support for a batch of new devices, while follow-up 2026.11.1 (released 2026-11-07) focuses on dashboard and chart improvements plus regression fixes. Both were published by joserebelo on the project\'s Codeberg release page.","date":"2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Project","permalink":"/news/tags/project","description":"Posts about projects and their releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"Gadgetbridge","permalink":"/news/tags/gadgetbridge","description":"Posts about the Gadgetbridge smartwatch companion app"}],"readingTime":1.23,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Julien Antony","title":"Systems tinkerer","url":"https://seriousjul.github.io","page":{"permalink":"/news/authors/seriousjul"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/seriousjul"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/seriousjul.png","key":"seriousjul"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Gadgetbridge 2026.11.0 and 2026.11.1 land new device support and fixes","authors":["seriousjul"],"tags":["project","gadgetbridge"],"slug":"2026-11-11-gadgetbridge-november-stable-releases"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Egui 0.37.0 lands colored emoji and glyph rendering","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-egui-0370-colored-emojis"},"nextItem":{"title":"LlamaCPP 0.9.0 lands OCP FP8 and a local speech stack","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-llamacpp-090-fp8-speech"}},"content":"Gadgetbridge released two stable versions within the past month. 2026.11.0 (released 2026-11-03) adds initial support for a batch of new devices, while follow-up 2026.11.1 (released 2026-11-07) focuses on dashboard and chart improvements plus regression fixes. Both were published by joserebelo on the project\'s Codeberg release page.\\n\\n## Releases\\n\\n- 2026.11.0 stable released on 2026-11-03, adding initial support for Anker Soundcore Motion+ (R50i NC, V20i), Bettdow FB051 (MoYoung / Da Fit), Beurer BM59, BRAZ/7HARRY (FitPro), Casio GG-B100, and more, as listed in the release changelog. ([source](https://codeberg.org/Freeyourgadget/Gadgetbridge/releases/tag/2026.11.0))\\n- 2026.11.1 stable released on 2026-11-07 as a maintenance release fixing and improving dashboard, charts, and vendor integrations. ([source](https://codeberg.org/Freeyourgadget/Gadgetbridge/releases/tag/2026.11.1))\\n\\n## Fixes and other\\n\\n- 2026.11.1 fixes a crash on weather processing on Android below 13. ([source](https://codeberg.org/Freeyourgadget/Gadgetbridge/releases/tag/2026.11.1))\\n- 2026.11.1 fixes a regression in Garmin web request URL encoding and improves Zepp OS BTBR packet handling. ([source](https://codeberg.org/Freeyourgadget/Gadgetbridge/releases/tag/2026.11.1))\\n- 2026.11.1 improves dashboard and charts: centered axis labels, fixed widget management and tile reshuffling on long press, better large font support, awake sleep shown in the day widget, and theme colors applied to sleep chart widgets; it also fixes the Endurain SSO login callback and Health Connect skin temperature deltas. ([source](https://codeberg.org/Freeyourgadget/Gadgetbridge/releases/tag/2026.11.1))\\n\\n## Sources\\n\\n- https://codeberg.org/Freeyourgadget/Gadgetbridge/releases/tag/2026.11.0\\n- https://codeberg.org/Freeyourgadget/Gadgetbridge/releases/tag/2026.11.1"},{"id":"2026-11-11-llamacpp-090-fp8-speech","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-llamacpp-090-fp8-speech","editUrl":"https://github.com/SeriousJul/seriousjul.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-11-11-llamacpp-090-fp8-speech.mdx","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-11-llamacpp-090-fp8-speech.mdx","title":"LlamaCPP 0.9.0 lands OCP FP8 and a local speech stack","description":"llama.cpp v0.9.0 shipped on 4 November 2026, adding OCP FP8 E4M3 quantization, a flashattnext_rows op that makes the unified KV cache efficient for multi-sequence inference, and a generic batched tensor copy API. The release expands the audio stack with Chatterbox TTS, Nemotron 3.5 Transcribe and predefined Pocket TTS voices, adds four new architectures (Clover, Limite, Metis-1.6, Mistral Large 4), and bumps ggml to 0.29.0 with early NCCL multi-node tensor parallel. Community coverage on dev.to explored the new local speech stack and its limits on Windows.","date":"2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Project","permalink":"/news/tags/project","description":"Posts about projects and their releases"},{"inline":true,"label":"llamacpp","permalink":"/news/tags/llamacpp"}],"readingTime":1.96,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Julien Antony","title":"Systems tinkerer","url":"https://seriousjul.github.io","page":{"permalink":"/news/authors/seriousjul"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/seriousjul"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/seriousjul.png","key":"seriousjul"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"LlamaCPP 0.9.0 lands OCP FP8 and a local speech stack","authors":["seriousjul"],"tags":["project","llamacpp"],"slug":"2026-11-11-llamacpp-090-fp8-speech"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Gadgetbridge 2026.11.0 and 2026.11.1 land new device support and fixes","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-gadgetbridge-november-stable-releases"},"nextItem":{"title":"Ninfer4090 perplexity tool learns the fork KV dtypes","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-ninfer4090-ninfer-perplexity-kv-dtypes"}},"content":"llama.cpp v0.9.0 shipped on 4 November 2026, adding OCP FP8 E4M3 quantization, a flash_attn_ext_rows op that makes the unified KV cache efficient for multi-sequence inference, and a generic batched tensor copy API. The release expands the audio stack with Chatterbox TTS, Nemotron 3.5 Transcribe and predefined Pocket TTS voices, adds four new architectures (Clover, Limite, Metis-1.6, Mistral Large 4), and bumps ggml to 0.29.0 with early NCCL multi-node tensor parallel. Community coverage on dev.to explored the new local speech stack and its limits on Windows.\\n\\n## Releases\\n- v0.9.0 was released on 2026-11-04 as the latest stable version of llama.cpp. It adds OCP FP8 E4M3 quantization support, the new flash_attn_ext_rows op, a batched tensor copy API, and major prefill optimizations for Gemma 4 E2B/E4B models. ([source](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/tag/v0.9.0))\\n- v0.9.0 updates ggml to v0.29.0, bringing early NCCL multi-node tensor parallel support. ([source](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/tag/v0.9.0))\\n\\n## Features\\n- v0.9.0 adds first-class Chatterbox TTS, Nemotron 3.5 Transcribe and predefined Pocket TTS voices, extending audio generation and transcription in the toolchain. ([source](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/tag/v0.9.0))\\n- v0.9.0 adds four new model architectures: Clover, Limite, Metis-1.6 and Mistral Large 4. ([source](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/tag/v0.9.0))\\n- Nightly build b12191 (2026-11-07) introduces a --moe-cache-cpu-share parameter that lets a fraction of Mixture-of-Experts cache misses be computed on the host CPU instead of the primary device, plus a new moe-cache-tune.py script to profile and recommend --moe-cache-mib and CPU share settings. ([source](https://aiunderstanding.org/news/llama-cpp-introduces-cpu-offloading-for-mixture-of-experts-cache-misses))\\n\\n## Community\\n- A dev.to article posted on 2026-11-05 details how v0.9.0\'s llama-tts tool and multimodal server support make Chatterbox TTS and Nemotron Transcribe usable as a fully local speech stack, and notes that Windows capture-path latency still limits real-time audio. ([source](https://dev.to/madnessbrains_i/llamacpp-090-ships-chatterbox-tts-and-ocp-fp8-local-speech-still-dies-on-the-windows-capture-10n0))\\n\\n## Sources\\n- https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/tag/v0.9.0\\n- https://dev.to/madnessbrains_i/llamacpp-090-ships-chatterbox-tts-and-ocp-fp8-local-speech-still-dies-on-the-windows-capture-10n0\\n- https://aiunderstanding.org/news/llama-cpp-introduces-cpu-offloading-for-mixture-of-experts-cache-misses"},{"id":"2026-11-11-ninfer4090-ninfer-perplexity-kv-dtypes","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-ninfer4090-ninfer-perplexity-kv-dtypes","editUrl":"https://github.com/SeriousJul/seriousjul.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-11-11-ninfer4090-ninfer-perplexity-kv-dtypes.mdx","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-11-ninfer4090-ninfer-perplexity-kv-dtypes.mdx","title":"Ninfer4090 perplexity tool learns the fork KV dtypes","description":"Ninfer4090\'s perplexity evaluator gained support for the fork\'s KV dtypes on 2026-10-24, finally allowing perplexity to be measured for the production 4-bit KV mode. The same day brought a small frontend validation fix and a community triage round recorded in the project ledger.","date":"2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Project","permalink":"/news/tags/project","description":"Posts about projects and their releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"Ninfer4090","permalink":"/news/tags/ninfer4090","description":"Posts about the Ninfer4090 local LLM inference project"}],"readingTime":1.04,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Julien Antony","title":"Systems tinkerer","url":"https://seriousjul.github.io","page":{"permalink":"/news/authors/seriousjul"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/seriousjul"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/seriousjul.png","key":"seriousjul"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Ninfer4090 perplexity tool learns the fork KV dtypes","authors":["seriousjul"],"tags":["project","ninfer4090"],"slug":"2026-11-11-ninfer4090-ninfer-perplexity-kv-dtypes"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"LlamaCPP 0.9.0 lands OCP FP8 and a local speech stack","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-llamacpp-090-fp8-speech"},"nextItem":{"title":"Omarchy 4.5 lands with desktop mode and Apple Silicon support","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-omarchy-4-5-released"}},"content":"Ninfer4090\'s perplexity evaluator gained support for the fork\'s KV dtypes on 2026-10-24, finally allowing perplexity to be measured for the production 4-bit KV mode. The same day brought a small frontend validation fix and a community triage round recorded in the project ledger.\\n\\n## Features\\n- ninfer-perplexity now accepts rk8v4, rk4v4, rk4v4-e8 and rk2v4-e8 KV dtypes (parser hunk from T-Crypt\'s PR #16). Previously it only parsed bf16, int8, fp8, nvfp4 and k8v4, so the production KV mode (rk4v4-e8) had no perplexity number. First used in the 2026-10-24 triage baseline on the v2 artifact: A16 4.363573 vs INT8 4.358936 on the quick corpus. Source: https://github.com/sergiuszm/ninfer-4090/commit/f3f4579ccd45139329fc40a8d7362d817f05d059\\n\\n## Fixes and other\\n- Frontend fix by laurinius (committed 2026-10-24) validates thinking control input to disallow the reasoning close marker, touching frontend.cpp and a test file. Source: https://github.com/sergiuszm/ninfer-4090/commit/0d9fce61cdb9523d31d3822267ec5b417f5f84ce\\n\\n## Community\\n- A docs commit on 2026-10-24 records the community triage round in docs/maintainer/port-ledger.md, alongside the perplexity and frontend changes. Source: https://github.com/sergiuszm/ninfer-4090/commit/7f47a62282b8e9d3c3b03bd6750d0bfe37e9bb66\\n\\n## Sources\\n- https://github.com/sergiuszm/ninfer-4090/commit/f3f4579ccd45139329fc40a8d7362d817f05d059\\n- https://github.com/sergiuszm/ninfer-4090/commit/0d9fce61cdb9523d31d3822267ec5b417f5f84ce\\n- https://github.com/sergiuszm/ninfer-4090/commit/7f47a62282b8e9d3c3b03bd6750d0bfe37e9bb66"},{"id":"2026-11-11-omarchy-4-5-released","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-omarchy-4-5-released","editUrl":"https://github.com/SeriousJul/seriousjul.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-11-11-omarchy-4-5-released.mdx","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-11-omarchy-4-5-released.mdx","title":"Omarchy 4.5 lands with desktop mode and Apple Silicon support","description":"Omarchy 4.5 (codenamed Quattro RS) shipped on November 5, 2026 as the project\'s first big feature release since Quattro, after more than 740 pull requests from 180+ contributors in twelve weeks. The headline changes: a traditional desktop mode alongside the tiling default, native installation on Apple Silicon MacBooks (M1/M2/M3/Neo), and interface support for 50 languages. The project also expanded beyond x86_64 for the first time, with reported support for NVIDIA N1X laptops and DGX Spark, while Snapdragon X laptop support is forthcoming.","date":"2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Project","permalink":"/news/tags/project","description":"Posts about projects and their releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"Omarchy","permalink":"/news/tags/omarchy","description":"Posts about the Omarchy Linux distribution"}],"readingTime":1.82,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Julien Antony","title":"Systems tinkerer","url":"https://seriousjul.github.io","page":{"permalink":"/news/authors/seriousjul"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/seriousjul"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/seriousjul.png","key":"seriousjul"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Omarchy 4.5 lands with desktop mode and Apple Silicon support","authors":["seriousjul"],"tags":["project","omarchy"],"slug":"2026-11-11-omarchy-4-5-released"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Ninfer4090 perplexity tool learns the fork KV dtypes","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-ninfer4090-ninfer-perplexity-kv-dtypes"},"nextItem":{"title":"Omarchy Core grows: Alcantara and Skyum join, Greptile becomes Distinguished Corporate Patron","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-omarchy-core-grows"}},"content":"Omarchy 4.5 (codenamed Quattro RS) shipped on November 5, 2026 as the project\'s first big feature release since Quattro, after more than 740 pull requests from 180+ contributors in twelve weeks. The headline changes: a traditional desktop mode alongside the tiling default, native installation on Apple Silicon MacBooks (M1/M2/M3/Neo), and interface support for 50 languages. The project also expanded beyond x86_64 for the first time, with reported support for NVIDIA N1X laptops and DGX Spark, while Snapdragon X laptop support is forthcoming.\\n\\n## Releases\\n\\n- Omarchy v4.5.0 (Quattro RS) was released to GitHub on November 5, 2026: the first major feature release since Quattro, adding a traditional desktop mode next to the tiling default, a native installer for M1/M2/M3/Neo MacBooks, and 50 languages ([source](https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/releases/tag/v4.5.0)).\\n- The release was announced on the project\'s news page on November 4, 2026, with instructions for existing users (Update > Omarchy) and a direct download for new machines ([source](https://omarchy.org/news/2026/11/omarchy-4-5/)).\\n\\n## Features\\n\\n- Floating workspaces with a dock: Super + L cycles any workspace between tiling, scrolling, and floating; floating windows get themed titlebars, a dock of pinned and running apps, and Super + M minimizes to the dock ([source](https://omarchy.org/news/2026/11/omarchy-4-5/)).\\n- Native Apple Silicon support: the Omarchy M team shipped a native Mac installer for M1/M2/M3/Neo MacBooks, building on Asahi Linux work ([source](https://omarchy.org/news/2026/11/omarchy-4-5/)).\\n- First multi-architecture release: beyond x86_64, Phoronix reports support for Apple Silicon hardware, NVIDIA N1X laptops, and DGX Spark desktops, with Snapdragon X support planned ([source](https://www.phoronix.com/news/Omarchy-4.5-Released)).\\n- More desktop customizations, including per-monitor workspaces, rebuilt notifications, an Appearance menu, and four new default apps (Hype, Monologue, Signed, Disktree), plus 50 languages ([source](https://omarchy.org/news/2026/11/omarchy-4-5/)).\\n\\n## Community\\n\\n- Phoronix covered the release on November 5, 2026, highlighting the distro\'s expansion beyond x86_64 and its new desktop customization options ([source](https://www.phoronix.com/news/Omarchy-4.5-Released)).\\n\\n## Sources\\n\\n- https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/releases/tag/v4.5.0\\n- https://omarchy.org/news/2026/11/omarchy-4-5/\\n- https://www.phoronix.com/news/Omarchy-4.5-Released"},{"id":"2026-11-11-omarchy-core-grows","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-omarchy-core-grows","editUrl":"https://github.com/SeriousJul/seriousjul.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-11-11-omarchy-core-grows.mdx","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-11-omarchy-core-grows.mdx","title":"Omarchy Core grows: Alcantara and Skyum join, Greptile becomes Distinguished Corporate Patron","description":"Omarchy announced major growth on its people side this month. Marcelo Alcantara and Birk Skyum, credited as two of the people doing the most to take Omarchy beyond x86, joined Omarchy Core on November 5. The Omacom Foundation also added Greptile as a Distinguished Corporate Patron (October 15) and hired HANCORE as Head of Design and Community (October 27).","date":"2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Project","permalink":"/news/tags/project","description":"Posts about projects and their releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"Omarchy","permalink":"/news/tags/omarchy","description":"Posts about the Omarchy Linux distribution"}],"readingTime":1.65,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Julien Antony","title":"Systems tinkerer","url":"https://seriousjul.github.io","page":{"permalink":"/news/authors/seriousjul"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/seriousjul"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/seriousjul.png","key":"seriousjul"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Omarchy Core grows: Alcantara and Skyum join, Greptile becomes Distinguished Corporate Patron","authors":["seriousjul"],"tags":["project","omarchy"],"slug":"2026-11-11-omarchy-core-grows"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Omarchy 4.5 lands with desktop mode and Apple Silicon support","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-omarchy-4-5-released"},"nextItem":{"title":"OmniRoute ships stable releases v3.8.53 and v3.8.52","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-omniroute-stable-releases"}},"content":"Omarchy announced major growth on its people side this month. Marcelo Alcantara and Birk Skyum, credited as two of the people doing the most to take Omarchy beyond x86, joined Omarchy Core on November 5. The Omacom Foundation also added Greptile as a Distinguished Corporate Patron (October 15) and hired HANCORE as Head of Design and Community (October 27).\\n\\n## Community\\n\\n- On November 5, 2026, Omarchy announced that Marcelo Alcantara and Birk Skyum are joining Omarchy Core. Alcantara coordinated the Omarchy M effort, a sixteen-person team that shipped the native macOS installer in Omarchy 4.5, letting Omarchy run alongside macOS on Apple Silicon Macs; Skyum\'s work on Omarchy Dragon is also highlighted in the post. Source: https://omarchy.org/news/2026/11/marcelo-alcantara-and-birk-skyum-join-omarchy-core/\\n- On October 15, 2026, the Omacom Foundation announced Greptile as a Distinguished Corporate Patron, contributing $150,000 in tokens for its PR review service so every pull request coming into Omarchy can be reviewed. The post notes Greptile has already reviewed almost 1,500 pull requests, and that across the 60 most recently merged PRs it reviewed, it flagged 39 issues it rated as serious, including a Turkish-locale lowercasing bug in laptop model matching. Source: https://omarchy.org/news/2026/10/greptile-joins-as-a-distinguished-corporate-patron/\\n- On October 27, 2026, the Omacom Foundation announced it is hiring HANCORE as Head of Design and Community, making him its fourth staff member alongside Krzysztof on Kernel, outfoxxed on Shell, and Emir on Infrastructure. He moves from his Omarchy AIR residency seat, where he started the plugin marketplace that grew into the official plugin catalogue with six thousand plugins, and whose themes (Solitude and Last Horizon) ship with Omarchy. Source: https://omarchy.org/news/2026/10/omacom-foundation-hires-hancore/\\n\\n## Sources\\n\\n- https://omarchy.org/news/2026/11/marcelo-alcantara-and-birk-skyum-join-omarchy-core/\\n- https://omarchy.org/news/2026/10/greptile-joins-as-a-distinguished-corporate-patron/\\n- https://omarchy.org/news/2026/10/omacom-foundation-hires-hancore/"},{"id":"2026-11-11-omniroute-stable-releases","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-omniroute-stable-releases","editUrl":"https://github.com/SeriousJul/seriousjul.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-11-11-omniroute-stable-releases.mdx","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-11-omniroute-stable-releases.mdx","title":"OmniRoute ships stable releases v3.8.53 and v3.8.52","description":"OmniRoute shipped two stable releases in this window: v3.8.52 on 2026-10-19 and v3.8.53 on 2026-11-06, the latter now marked as the latest release. Both carried large documented changelogs with attached release notes and credited large contributor bases.","date":"2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Project","permalink":"/news/tags/project","description":"Posts about projects and their releases"},{"inline":true,"label":"omniroute","permalink":"/news/tags/omniroute"}],"readingTime":0.92,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Julien Antony","title":"Systems tinkerer","url":"https://seriousjul.github.io","page":{"permalink":"/news/authors/seriousjul"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/seriousjul"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/seriousjul.png","key":"seriousjul"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"OmniRoute ships stable releases v3.8.53 and v3.8.52","authors":["seriousjul"],"tags":["project","omniroute"],"slug":"2026-11-11-omniroute-stable-releases"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Omarchy Core grows: Alcantara and Skyum join, Greptile becomes Distinguished Corporate Patron","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-omarchy-core-grows"},"nextItem":{"title":"Strata 0.2.13 lands Strix Halo launch fix and DFlash2 defaults","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-strata-0213-strix-halo-fix"}},"content":"OmniRoute shipped two stable releases in this window: v3.8.52 on 2026-10-19 and v3.8.53 on 2026-11-06, the latter now marked as the latest release. Both carried large documented changelogs with attached release notes and credited large contributor bases.\\n\\n## Releases\\n\\n- v3.8.53 (2026-11-06): shipped as a stable release and is currently the latest; it includes 1,189 documented changes from 1,162 commits, with complete notes attached as CHANGELOG-v3.8.53.md. Source: https://github.com/cheaper-inference/OmniRoute/releases/tag/v3.8.53\\n- v3.8.52 (2026-10-19): published as a stable release with 1,442 documented changes (135 features, 1,112 fixes, 195 maintenance entries) from 1,386 commits, with full notes attached as CHANGELOG-v3.8.52.md. Source: https://github.com/cheaper-inference/OmniRoute/releases/tag/v3.8.52\\n\\n## Community\\n\\n- The release pages for v3.8.52 (2026-10-19) and v3.8.53 (2026-11-06) thank their contributor bases: 306 external contributors for v3.8.52 and 222 people contributing to v3.8.53. Sources: https://github.com/cheaper-inference/OmniRoute/releases/tag/v3.8.52, https://github.com/cheaper-inference/OmniRoute/releases/tag/v3.8.53\\n\\n## Sources\\n\\n- https://github.com/cheaper-inference/OmniRoute/releases/tag/v3.8.52\\n- https://github.com/cheaper-inference/OmniRoute/releases/tag/v3.8.53"},{"id":"2026-11-11-strata-0213-strix-halo-fix","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-strata-0213-strix-halo-fix","editUrl":"https://github.com/SeriousJul/seriousjul.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-11-11-strata-0213-strix-halo-fix.mdx","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-11-strata-0213-strix-halo-fix.mdx","title":"Strata 0.2.13 lands Strix Halo launch fix and DFlash2 defaults","description":"Strata 0.2.13 (engine 0.1.59) shipped on November 9, 2026 with new per-card DFlash2 drafting defaults, a much faster app start, an Intel Arc determinism fix, a Linux expert-store loading fix, and groundwork for Qwen4. Press coverage highlights the Strix Halo Terminal launch fix, which cut startup from up to about 10 minutes to 60-85 seconds, and notes the project has passed 42,000 GitHub stars.","date":"2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Project","permalink":"/news/tags/project","description":"Posts about projects and their releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"Strata","permalink":"/news/tags/strata","description":"Posts about the Strata local LLM engine"}],"readingTime":1.3,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Julien Antony","title":"Systems tinkerer","url":"https://seriousjul.github.io","page":{"permalink":"/news/authors/seriousjul"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/seriousjul"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/seriousjul.png","key":"seriousjul"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Strata 0.2.13 lands Strix Halo launch fix and DFlash2 defaults","authors":["seriousjul"],"tags":["project","strata"],"slug":"2026-11-11-strata-0213-strix-halo-fix"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"OmniRoute ships stable releases v3.8.53 and v3.8.52","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-omniroute-stable-releases"},"nextItem":{"title":"Gadgetbridge 2026.11.1 stable lands with widget and Garmin fixes","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-gadgetbridge-2026-11-1-stable"}},"content":"Strata 0.2.13 (engine 0.1.59) shipped on November 9, 2026 with new per-card DFlash2 drafting defaults, a much faster app start, an Intel Arc determinism fix, a Linux expert-store loading fix, and groundwork for Qwen4. Press coverage highlights the Strix Halo Terminal launch fix, which cut startup from up to about 10 minutes to 60-85 seconds, and notes the project has passed 42,000 GitHub stars.\\n\\n## Releases\\n- Strata 0.2.13 released on 2026-11-09 (app and Terminal 0.2.13, Control and all engine packages 0.1.59; DGX Spark also receives 0.2.13). The update brings new card-specific DFlash2 drafting defaults (49.1 tok/s on Strix Halo, +5.2%), a faster app start, and Qwen4 groundwork: [release notes](https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/releases/tag/v0.2.13).\\n\\n## Fixes and other\\n- The release includes a Strix Halo Terminal launch fix reducing startup from up to ~594 s to 60-85 s, an Intel Arc determinism fix, and a fix for broken Linux expert-store loading, plus follow-up 0.2.13.1 letting the Linux desktop app set up models on Intel Arc cards: [release notes](https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/releases/tag/v0.2.13).\\n\\n## Community\\n- Linux Compatible covered the 0.2.13 release on 2026-11-09, calling it the most practical update yet to the engine and noting Strata has climbed past 42,000 GitHub stars: [article](https://www.linuxcompatible.org/story/strata-0213-strix-halo-launch-fix-and-qwen4-prep-for-the-125b-consumerpc-llm-engine/).\\n\\n## Sources\\n- https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/releases/tag/v0.2.13\\n- https://www.linuxcompatible.org/story/strata-0213-strix-halo-launch-fix-and-qwen4-prep-for-the-125b-consumerpc-llm-engine/"},{"id":"2026-11-11-gadgetbridge-2026-11-1-stable","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-gadgetbridge-2026-11-1-stable","editUrl":"https://github.com/SeriousJul/seriousjul.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-11-11-gadgetbridge-2026-11-1-stable.mdx","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-11-gadgetbridge-2026-11-1-stable.mdx","title":"Gadgetbridge 2026.11.1 stable lands with widget and Garmin fixes","description":"Gadgetbridge shipped stable release 2026.11.1 on 2026-11-07, a point release focused on dashboard widgets, sleep/HRV chart polish, and several device and platform fixes. The same week, version 2026.11.0 (build 256) appeared as a suggested update on F-Droid, where its release notes highlight 25 new plus 21 experimental devices and a refreshed design.","date":"2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Project","permalink":"/news/tags/project","description":"Posts about projects and their releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"Gadgetbridge","permalink":"/news/tags/gadgetbridge","description":"Posts about the Gadgetbridge smartwatch companion app"}],"readingTime":1.06,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Julien Antony","title":"Systems tinkerer","url":"https://seriousjul.github.io","page":{"permalink":"/news/authors/seriousjul"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/seriousjul"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/seriousjul.png","key":"seriousjul"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Gadgetbridge 2026.11.1 stable lands with widget and Garmin fixes","authors":["seriousjul"],"tags":["project","gadgetbridge"],"slug":"2026-11-11-gadgetbridge-2026-11-1-stable"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Strata 0.2.13 lands Strix Halo launch fix and DFlash2 defaults","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-strata-0213-strix-halo-fix"},"nextItem":{"title":"Egui 0.37.0 lands colored emoji support","permalink":"/news/2026-10-18-egui-egui-0370-emoji-release"}},"content":"Gadgetbridge shipped stable release 2026.11.1 on 2026-11-07, a point release focused on dashboard widgets, sleep/HRV chart polish, and several device and platform fixes. The same week, version 2026.11.0 (build 256) appeared as a suggested update on F-Droid, where its release notes highlight 25 new plus 21 experimental devices and a refreshed design.\\n\\n## Releases\\n- 2026.11.1 stable was released by joserebelo on 2026-11-07. The changelog covers dashboard widget fixes and improvements (manage widgets setting, tile reshuffling, large font support, theme colors for sleep/HRV charts), Endurain SSO login callback fix, a weather-processing crash fix on Android < 13, a Garmin web request URL-encoding regression fix, Health Connect skin-temperature delta correction, and improved Zepp OS BTBR packet handling. ([source](https://codeberg.org/Freeyourgadget/Gadgetbridge/releases/tag/2026.11.1))\\n\\n## Community\\n- On 2026-11-06 the F-Droid repository listed Gadgetbridge 2026.11.0 (build 256) as a suggested update, with release highlights including support for 25 new plus 21 experimental devices, a refreshed design for dashboard, charts, and alarms, device cards, a workouts tab, Garmin import from the official app, and multiple fixes for charts, Health Connect, Huami, Xiaomi, and Zepp OS. ([source](https://f-droid.org/packages/nodomain.freeyourgadget.gadgetbridge/))\\n\\n## Sources\\n- https://codeberg.org/Freeyourgadget/Gadgetbridge/releases/tag/2026.11.1\\n- https://f-droid.org/packages/nodomain.freeyourgadget.gadgetbridge/"},{"id":"2026-10-18-egui-egui-0370-emoji-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026-10-18-egui-egui-0370-emoji-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/SeriousJul/seriousjul.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-10-18-egui-egui-0370-emoji-release.mdx","source":"@site/blog/2026-10-18-egui-egui-0370-emoji-release.mdx","title":"Egui 0.37.0 lands colored emoji support","description":"Egui 0.37.0, titled \\"Colored emojis!\\", was released on 2026-10-15 and is the first release to ship full emoji and glyph support via a new glyph rasterizer and font provider API. The same release adds a CompletionPopup autocomplete widget and an experimental theme plugin system, alongside improved AccessKit accessibility, video recording of integration tests, and breaking changes for API users.","date":"2026-10-18T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Project","permalink":"/news/tags/project","description":"Posts about projects and their releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"egui","permalink":"/news/tags/egui","description":"Posts about the egui GUI framework"}],"readingTime":1.23,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Julien Antony","title":"Systems tinkerer","url":"https://seriousjul.github.io","page":{"permalink":"/news/authors/seriousjul"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/seriousjul"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/seriousjul.png","key":"seriousjul"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Egui 0.37.0 lands colored emoji support","authors":["seriousjul"],"tags":["project","egui"],"slug":"2026-10-18-egui-egui-0370-emoji-release"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Gadgetbridge 2026.11.1 stable lands with widget and Garmin fixes","permalink":"/news/2026-11-11-gadgetbridge-2026-11-1-stable"},"nextItem":{"title":"n8n 2.43.7 stable lands execution suspension as ZoomInfo ships native node","permalink":"/news/2026-10-18-n8n-n8n-2-43-7-zoominfo-integration"}},"content":"Egui 0.37.0, titled \\"Colored emojis!\\", was released on 2026-10-15 and is the first release to ship full emoji and glyph support via a new glyph rasterizer and font provider API. The same release adds a CompletionPopup autocomplete widget and an experimental theme plugin system, alongside improved AccessKit accessibility, video recording of integration tests, and breaking changes for API users.\\n\\n## Releases\\n- On 2026-10-15, egui released stable version 0.37.0 (\\"Colored emojis!\\") featuring full emoji and glyph support through a new glyph rasterizer/font provider API, a CompletionPopup autocomplete widget, an experimental theme plugin system, improved AccessKit accessibility, and video recording of integration tests ([source](https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0)).\\n\\n## Features\\n- Full colored emoji and glyph support via a new glyph rasterizer and font provider API, introduced in 0.37.0 on 2026-10-15 ([source](https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0)).\\n- New CompletionPopup autocomplete widget in 0.37.0, released 2026-10-15 ([source](https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0)).\\n- Experimental theme plugin system shipped in 0.37.0 on 2026-10-15 ([source](https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0)).\\n- Improved accessibility through AccessKit and video recording of integration tests, both in 0.37.0 on 2026-10-15 ([source](https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0)).\\n\\n## Fixes and other\\n- Breaking changes in 0.37.0 (2026-10-15): the AsId trait was removed and default_fonts was dropped from the default feature set ([source](https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0)).\\n\\n## Sources\\n- https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0"},{"id":"2026-10-18-n8n-n8n-2-43-7-zoominfo-integration","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026-10-18-n8n-n8n-2-43-7-zoominfo-integration","editUrl":"https://github.com/SeriousJul/seriousjul.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-10-18-n8n-n8n-2-43-7-zoominfo-integration.mdx","source":"@site/blog/2026-10-18-n8n-n8n-2-43-7-zoominfo-integration.mdx","title":"n8n 2.43.7 stable lands execution suspension as ZoomInfo ships native node","description":"n8n shipped four releases between Oct 14 and Oct 16, led by stable 2.43.7, which can now suspend in-flight production executions when a worker shuts down. The biggest ecosystem news came from ZoomInfo, which launched a verified native n8n node exposing its GTM Context Graph for workflows and AI agents.","date":"2026-10-18T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Project","permalink":"/news/tags/project","description":"Posts about projects and their releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"n8n","permalink":"/news/tags/n8n","description":"Posts about the n8n workflow automation tool"}],"readingTime":1.73,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Julien Antony","title":"Systems tinkerer","url":"https://seriousjul.github.io","page":{"permalink":"/news/authors/seriousjul"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/seriousjul"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/seriousjul.png","key":"seriousjul"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"n8n 2.43.7 stable lands execution suspension as ZoomInfo ships native node","authors":["seriousjul"],"tags":["project","n8n"],"slug":"2026-10-18-n8n-n8n-2-43-7-zoominfo-integration"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Egui 0.37.0 lands colored emoji support","permalink":"/news/2026-10-18-egui-egui-0370-emoji-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Omarchy 4.0.5 ships Qt 6.12 and BORE-scheduler kernel","permalink":"/news/2026-10-18-omarchy-omarchy-4-0-5-release"}},"content":"n8n shipped four releases between Oct 14 and Oct 16, led by stable 2.43.7, which can now suspend in-flight production executions when a worker shuts down. The biggest ecosystem news came from ZoomInfo, which launched a verified native n8n node exposing its GTM Context Graph for workflows and AI agents.\\n\\n## Releases\\n\\n- 2026-10-16: n8n 2.43.7 (latest stable) released, adding the ability to suspend in-flight production executions at worker shutdown in core. [Release](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/releases/tag/n8n%402.43.7)\\n- 2026-10-15: n8n 2.43.6 released with a core fix creating a fresh XML parser for each webhook request body. [Release](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/releases/tag/n8n%402.43.6)\\n- 2026-10-14: n8n 2.43.5 released, showing Gemini models by name and listing prioritized models first in model pickers. [Release](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/releases/tag/n8n%402.43.5)\\n- 2026-10-14: n8n 1.123.85, a routine maintenance release for the legacy 1.x branch with no notable changes listed. [Release](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/releases/tag/n8n%401.123.85)\\n\\n## Features\\n\\n- 2026-10-12: ZoomInfo announced a native, verified ZoomInfo node inside n8n, built and maintained by ZoomInfo. Once a workflow authenticates with a customer\'s own ZoomInfo credentials, it can search contacts and companies, enrich records, and monitor buying-signal and intent data from ZoomInfo\'s GTM Context Graph via GTM.AI. [Announcement](https://ir.zoominfo.com/news-releases/news-release-details/zoominfo-launches-native-integration-n8n-through-gtmai/)\\n\\n## Fixes and other\\n\\n- 2026-10-15: Webhook XML parsing fixed in 2.43.6 by creating a fresh XML parser for each request body. [Release](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/releases/tag/n8n%402.43.6)\\n- 2026-10-14: chunk() expression extension now validates its size argument, shipped in 2.43.5. [Release](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/releases/tag/n8n%402.43.5)\\n\\n## Sources\\n\\n- https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/releases/tag/n8n%402.43.7\\n- https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/releases/tag/n8n%402.43.6\\n- https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/releases/tag/n8n%402.43.5\\n- https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/releases/tag/n8n%401.123.85\\n- https://ir.zoominfo.com/news-releases/news-release-details/zoominfo-launches-native-integration-n8n-through-gtmai/"},{"id":"2026-10-18-omarchy-omarchy-4-0-5-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026-10-18-omarchy-omarchy-4-0-5-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/SeriousJul/seriousjul.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-10-18-omarchy-omarchy-4-0-5-release.mdx","source":"@site/blog/2026-10-18-omarchy-omarchy-4-0-5-release.mdx","title":"Omarchy 4.0.5 ships Qt 6.12 and BORE-scheduler kernel","description":"Omarchy 4.0.5 was released on 18 October 2026 as a stable point release bringing fixes and refinements ahead of the next feature release. The update moves the distro onto the Qt 6.12 toolkit, bumps stable-ring packages, and ships an updated Linux 7.2 stable kernel with the BORE scheduler. Phoronix also covered the release, highlighting millisecond-level optimization of web browser launch by avoiding XDG overhead.","date":"2026-10-18T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Project","permalink":"/news/tags/project","description":"Posts about projects and their releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"Omarchy","permalink":"/news/tags/omarchy","description":"Posts about the Omarchy Linux distribution"}],"readingTime":1.2,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Julien Antony","title":"Systems tinkerer","url":"https://seriousjul.github.io","page":{"permalink":"/news/authors/seriousjul"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/seriousjul"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/seriousjul.png","key":"seriousjul"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Omarchy 4.0.5 ships Qt 6.12 and BORE-scheduler kernel","authors":["seriousjul"],"tags":["project","omarchy"],"slug":"2026-10-18-omarchy-omarchy-4-0-5-release"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"n8n 2.43.7 stable lands execution suspension as ZoomInfo ships native node","permalink":"/news/2026-10-18-n8n-n8n-2-43-7-zoominfo-integration"},"nextItem":{"title":"Strata 0.1.45 adds picture reading and parallel serving","permalink":"/news/2026-10-18-strata-strata-0145-parallel-speedups"}},"content":"Omarchy 4.0.5 was released on 18 October 2026 as a stable point release bringing fixes and refinements ahead of the next feature release. The update moves the distro onto the Qt 6.12 toolkit, bumps stable-ring packages, and ships an updated Linux 7.2 stable kernel with the BORE scheduler. Phoronix also covered the release, highlighting millisecond-level optimization of web browser launch by avoiding XDG overhead.\\n\\n## Releases\\n- v4.0.5 (stable) released on 18 Oct 2026, with a set of fixes and refinements, a move to Qt 6.12, stable-ring package bumps, and an updated kernel with the BORE scheduler; existing machines can upgrade via Update > Omarchy and new installs use the 4.0.5 ISO ([GitHub release](https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/releases/tag/v4.0.5))\\n\\n## Features\\n- Faster default web browser launch via millisecond-level optimization that avoids the xdg-settings get default-web-browser overhead, as reported on the 4.0.5 release (18 Oct 2026) ([Phoronix](https://www.phoronix.com/news/Omarchy-Faster-Web-Browser))\\n\\n## Fixes and other\\n- Improved reliability of Wi-Fi QR code generation among other fixes in v4.0.5 (18 Oct 2026) ([GitHub release](https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/releases/tag/v4.0.5))\\n\\n## Community\\n- Phoronix (Michael Larabel) covered the 4.0.5 release on 18 Oct 2026, noting it pulls in the Linux 7.2 stable kernel with BORE scheduler and Qt 6.12 updates alongside smaller improvements ([Phoronix](https://www.phoronix.com/news/Omarchy-Faster-Web-Browser))\\n\\n## Sources\\n- https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/releases/tag/v4.0.5\\n- https://www.phoronix.com/news/Omarchy-Faster-Web-Browser"},{"id":"2026-10-18-strata-strata-0145-parallel-speedups","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026-10-18-strata-strata-0145-parallel-speedups","editUrl":"https://github.com/SeriousJul/seriousjul.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-10-18-strata-strata-0145-parallel-speedups.mdx","source":"@site/blog/2026-10-18-strata-strata-0145-parallel-speedups.mdx","title":"Strata 0.1.45 adds picture reading and parallel serving","description":"Strata v0.1.45 shipped on October 17, 2026, bringing picture reading to Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, concurrent request serving via --parallel (up to ~40% faster on tested GPUs), and opt-in switches for multi-user servers. Qwen3.8-Flash-Next answers remain byte-identical to 0.1.44.1. A r/LocalLLaMA thread also discussed Qwen3.8-Flash-Next with user reports of testing Strata.","date":"2026-10-18T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Project","permalink":"/news/tags/project","description":"Posts about projects and their releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"Strata","permalink":"/news/tags/strata","description":"Posts about the Strata local LLM engine"}],"readingTime":1.95,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Julien Antony","title":"Systems tinkerer","url":"https://seriousjul.github.io","page":{"permalink":"/news/authors/seriousjul"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/seriousjul"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/seriousjul.png","key":"seriousjul"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Strata 0.1.45 adds picture reading and parallel serving","authors":["seriousjul"],"tags":["project","strata"],"slug":"2026-10-18-strata-strata-0145-parallel-speedups"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Omarchy 4.0.5 ships Qt 6.12 and BORE-scheduler kernel","permalink":"/news/2026-10-18-omarchy-omarchy-4-0-5-release"}},"content":"Strata v0.1.45 shipped on October 17, 2026, bringing picture reading to Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, concurrent request serving via --parallel (up to ~40% faster on tested GPUs), and opt-in switches for multi-user servers. Qwen3.8-Flash-Next answers remain byte-identical to 0.1.44.1. A r/LocalLLaMA thread also discussed Qwen3.8-Flash-Next with user reports of testing Strata.\\n\\n## Releases\\n- **v0.1.45 released (2026-10-17)**: picture reading for Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, several concurrent requests at once, up to 40% faster runs on tested GPUs, switches for multi-user servers, and Mac and setup fixes. Update via `UPDATE.bat` (Linux: `./update.sh`); setup replaces the engine with 0.1.45. ([Source](https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/releases/tag/v0.1.45))\\n\\n## Features\\n- **Picture support for Qwen3.6-35B-A3B (v0.1.45, 2026-10-17)**: setup asks \\"Do you want images?\\" for Qwen3.6, downloads the pinned mmproj (~0.9 GB) and writes `--vision`; it uses the same image encoder family as Flash-Next, and output was checked against llama.cpp on the same pictures with teacher forcing. ([Source](https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/releases/tag/v0.1.45))\\n- **Concurrent requests (v0.1.45, 2026-10-17)**: the server now handles several requests at once via `--parallel` (up to 8 slots per the release notes), running up to ~40% faster on the GPUs tested. ([Source](https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/releases/tag/v0.1.45))\\n- **Multi-user server switches (v0.1.45, 2026-10-17)**: opt-in switches for running multi-user servers were added. ([Source](https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/releases/tag/v0.1.45))\\n\\n## Fixes and other\\n- **Mac and setup fixes (v0.1.45, 2026-10-17)**: routine Mac and setup fixes are bundled in the release. ([Source](https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/releases/tag/v0.1.45))\\n- **Identity guarantee for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (v0.1.45, 2026-10-17)**: answers of the Qwen3.8-Flash-Next models are byte-identical to 0.1.44.1 in the project\'s identity tests on every GPU machine tested (CUDA sm_60 / sm_86, HIP gfx1201, Intel A750, Mac M4). ([Source](https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/releases/tag/v0.1.45))\\n\\n## Community\\n- **r/LocalLLaMA thread on Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (2026-10-16)**: the discussion thread \\"I don\'t get the qwen 3.8 flash next hype\\" includes user reports of testing the model with Strata, with one user saying Strata results were worse than llama.cpp on their 4x 3090 setup despite faster generation. ([Source](https://www.reddit.com/r/LocalLLaMA/comments/1x7uf15/i_dont_get_the_qwen_38_flash_next_hype/))\\n\\n## Sources\\n- https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/releases/tag/v0.1.45\\n- https://www.reddit.com/r/LocalLLaMA/comments/1x7uf15/i_dont_get_the_qwen_38_flash_next_hype/"}]}}')}}]);